ong the San Juan River from the Four Corners through\nMexican Hat, UT. This includes Bluff, Montezuma Creek and Aneth.\n\n* WHEN...Until 515 PM MST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...River levels continue to rise due to excess runoff from\nSunday's rainfall. Expect high water levels and the River exceeding\nits banks, inundating low-lying areas along the San Juan River. A\nprolonged period of high water is forecast, with a crest near 23.5\nft Thursday morning. It will take several hours for all the water\nfrom these storms to work through local drainage systems.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1222 PM MST, stream gauge reports upstream and impacts of\nflooding have been reported along the San Juan River near\nFarmington, NM. Expect flood waters to reach the Four Corners\nWednesday evening and the town of Bluff early Thursday morning.\nTiming of crest is subject to change as more details become\navailable. Please continue to monitor the forecast and updated\nwarnings.\n- At 11:30 AM MST Monday the stage was 20.4 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 22.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river will rise to 22 feet late this evening with\na secondary crest near 23.5 feet expected near Bluff early\nThursday morning. It will then fall below flood stage Thursday\nmorning.\n- Flood stage is 23.0 feet.\n\n- Http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMexican Hat, Bluff, Montezuma Creek, and Aneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-05T17:15:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.00b8de8d3d582a70415755093091fe5b78bb2bcf.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.00b8de8d3d582a70415755093091fe5b78bb2bcf.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-04T05:10:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 040510 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1010 PM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Rivers and other waterways